--<<Object Steps>>:
--instSupport   															$*
-----Step 1:basic information
-----Step 2: for draw
-----Step 3:for recognising
-----Step 4:new way to instore parts of support
-----Step 5:old way to instore parts of support
-----Step 6:geometry things
-----Step 7:materials
-----Step 8:draw planes
--
--<<Method>>:
--<<Public method>>:
--instSupport(!item is any) 												$* initial method
--getsuppAttArr(!suppAtts is array) is array								$* public 	return array of attribution of support
--addtoview()   															$* public 	add pipe and support to view
--getSpecialMaterials(!atts is array) is array  							$* public 	get component materials
--sumMaterials(!inputatts is array) is array								$* public 	get sum materials
--getweldlist() is array													$* public, return array of list of weld, this method has to be modified
--
--Step 1:json
--getJsonData(!materialAttS is array, !materialAttShow is array, !suppAtts is array ,!suppAttShow is array) is array	$* public, return array of json data
--
--<<Private method>>:
--getspecialnum()   														$* it supposed to get nbbm
--getsuppfunction() 														$* get function of support
--getmaterial() 															$* get material of support
--getmaterialfrompart(!object is any) is array  							$* get array of material from one part object
--setMaterialSpecialNumber()												$* set component number
--getwelds()																$* get weld of support, but this method has to be modified
--getweldbetweenmems(!mem1 is string, !mem2 is string,!object is any) is array  	$* check if there is any weld between two partobjects, if yes, return array of points
--getparts()																$* get all part of support, and put them into partobjects, and get connections between them with mechanic method
--dealMechanics()   														$* 计算他们接触情况
--dealdisconnect()  														$* maybe some pane or atta are not considered, but they are useful, normally they are dealed in assignconnections
--checkdisconnect() 														$* check if any part of support does not connect to other part
--assignConnections()   													$* assign connection data in each part object
--------------Step 1:set partconnections
--------------Step 2:set partobject
--checkconnection(!x is real, !y is real, !reverse is boolean)  			$* check if two items are connected, if yes, add connection data into this partconnections
-----Step 1:clamp
--------Step 1:bolt
--------Step 2:connect
--------Step 3:beam
--------Step 4:pane
--------Step 5:panes
--------Step 6:tube
--addattatopartobjects()													$* add atta to partobjects
--------Step 1:get data of all atta with suppname from bran of curren atta, it
--dealattaparttype(!attaclass is array, !inputattadatas is array)   		$* put attadata into partobjects
--getattadatas(!atta is string) is array									$* get attadata from bran which is relevant to suppport
-----Step 1:got attas with suppname from bran
--------Step 1:if atta is point, add into pointattas, or if it is pad/lug/leg, then add into otherattas
-----------Step 3:if atta is pad, get array of padvolume, in order to identify group for attas
-----Step 2:check if lug/leg is on pad
-----Step 3:start to identify group
--------Step 1:check attsdata one by one, , it means they sould be in one group that their some attributes are some
--------Step 2:if some of them are in one group, put them into one element(array) of indices, like padindices/lugindices/legindices
-----Step 4:each element in padindices/legindices generate a element of attaclass
-----Step 5:check if two element in lugindices should in one group
--------Step 1:if two element in lugindices are on one pad, these two element generate one group attaclass
--------Step 2:if there are some lugs not sure they are in one group or not with other lugs
--------Step 3:use dir,bore and distance to identify
--------Step 4:find group with same dir bore and distance is near than tolerance distance
--------Step 5:consider each one ofrest lug as one group
--------Step 6:generate attaclass for each group
-----Step 6:return result: attadatas contains data for each atta,attaclass is group of indices of atta
-----Step 7:otherattas: all atta with geo, pointattas: all atta without geo
--addconcreteToPartobjects()												$* add concrete to partobject
--addselfToPartobjects()													$* add part of support to partobjects
--dealparttype(!item is string, !type is string )   						$* add item according type into partobjects
--getvalidmems(!item is any) is array   									$* get good items from catref
--checkvalid(!mem is any) is boolean										$* check if cata element is valid
--getLineData() is boolean  												$* old way to get geo data of support to draw
--draw()																	$* draw dim and mlabel
-----Step 1:new way
-----Step 2:old way
--deletestru()  															$* delete dim and mlabel
--clear()   																$* clear array of insupport, --------to be completed
--getName() is boolean  													$* get supp/stru/rest name and initial mbdstru of support
--uniquePoss(!poss is array) is array   									$*
--drawmaterial()															$*
--getnodenameforsupp()  													$* get node name of support
--getDimJson() is array 													$* get json data for dim and mlabel
--materialsJson(!materialAttS is array, !materialAttShow is array, !tryname is string) is array 	$* get json data of materials
--specialmaterialsJson(!materialAttS is array, !materialAttShow is array, !tryname is string ) is array 	$* get json data of component materials
--suppAttJson(!suppAtts is array, !suppAttShow is array, !tryname is string ) is array  	$* get json data of attribution
--weldJson(!tryname is string) is array 									$* get json data of weld
--getProofreadingJson(!tryname is string) is array  						$* get json data of proofreading
--getDrawingInfoJson(!tryname is string) is array   						$* get json data of drawing
